{
 "$schema": "../_format.schema.json",
 "format": "plx-ontology-domain/v1",
 "domain": "mission_control",
 "origin": "curated",
 "description": "Mission Control work records and brain knowledge as ontology objects: MCTask, MCApproval, MCBucket and MCTaskEvent from MC read tools, KnowledgeEntry from mc_search_knowledge, all captured by integrations/mc_sources.py into the versioned capture store (source mission_control, cited mc://<scope>/<collection>/<id>@<generation>-<capture>). Audience mc:<scope>/<collection>, plus /<project> for tasks, approvals, task events and buckets: an MC operator scope is what that operator's MC principal may see, MC scopes those per project (PLX_MC@eeb7db7 src/lib/permissions/project-acl.ts), and a reader sees a record only when the live audience grants it mc:<scope>:<collection> and, for those, mc:<scope>:project:<project> (the MC project id or unparented). These are work and knowledge records, never business facts. Identifiers written in task text, gate reasons and knowledge entries are stored lead links (MCTask.mentions_<type>, MCApproval.mentions_<type>, KnowledgeEntry.mentions_<type>, ontology/schema.py MC_MENTION_LINK_RULES). Approvable MC writes are action types written by ontology/generator/mcp.py from the pinned tool shapes (generated/meta/mcp_tools.json); do not edit them by hand.",
